### Auth Endpoint Changes (`backend/api/v1/auth.py`)

| Endpoint | Change |
|----------|--------|
| `POST /register` | Generates a secure 32-byte `secrets.token_urlsafe` token, stores in `verification_tokens` with 24h expiry, sends verification email. User is **not** logged in automatically. |
| `POST /login` | Now rejects unverified users with **HTTP 403** and a clear message. |
| `POST /verify-email` | **NEW** — accepts `{ token }`, marks user as verified, deletes all their tokens (single-use). Rejects expired tokens with 400. |
| `POST /resend-verification` | **NEW** — accepts `{ email }`, enforces 2-minute rate limit per user, generates fresh token, sends new email. Never reveals user existence. |
| `GET /me` | Updated `get_current_user` dependency to also check `is_verified`. |
| `POST /refresh` | Updated to also check `is_verified`. |

### Database (Supabase)

